From 2e7c89716688a3995eb5237190285ab9791fc286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: friedger <mail@friedger.de>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:57:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(auth): sign in through an upstream OpenID Provider

Authorization code + PKCE login against OIDC_ISSUER (Belfry: Authentik).
The callback verifies the ID token against the provider's JWKS (RS256 or
ES256; iss, aud, exp, nonce), maps the subject to an existing account and
sets the keycast_session cookie with a server-signed UCAN, then returns to
the OAuth authorize request (or the web app) where consent continues.

Accounts are never created here: the first login links the subject to the
account whose vine_id equals the OIDC_LINK_CLAIM claim (preloaded accounts
need no claim step); later logins use oidc_identities. The OAuth popup
shows a 'Sign in with ...' button; OIDC_HIDE_PASSWORD_LOGIN hides the
password and registration forms.
